      deepMeaning: "Momentum is one of the most fundamental conserved quantities in nature. By Noether's theorem, conservation of momentum is a direct consequence of the translational symmetry of space — the laws of physics are the same everywhere in space. This is a profound connection between symmetry and conservation laws. In relativistic mechanics, p = γmv, where γ is the Lorentz factor. At low speeds, γ ≈ 1 and the classical formula is recovered.",
