      deepMeaning: "This is an exact law of nature, valid in classical mechanics, quantum mechanics, special relativity, and quantum field theory. It is the most universally conserved quantity in physics. It applies regardless of whether the collision is elastic or inelastic, head-on or glancing, as long as the system is isolated from external forces. By Noether's theorem, it is a direct consequence of the spatial homogeneity of the universe — the laws of physics do not change from place to place.",
