      deepMeaning: "e = 1 means a perfectly elastic collision — kinetic energy is fully conserved. e = 0 means a perfectly inelastic collision — objects stick together and maximum kinetic energy is lost. Values between 0 and 1 describe real collisions where some kinetic energy is lost to heat, sound, and deformation. A rubber ball on a hard floor has e ≈ 0.8–0.9. A ball of clay has e ≈ 0. The coefficient is a material property that depends on both colliding objects.",
