      deepMeaning: "The center of mass is the point at which the entire mass of the system can be considered to be concentrated for the purpose of applying external forces. Newton's Second Law for a system becomes F_ext = M·a_cm, where M is total mass and a_cm is the acceleration of the center of mass. When no external forces act, the center of mass moves at constant velocity or stays at rest. This is why a thrown wrench rotates about its center of mass while the CM itself follows a perfect parabolic trajectory under gravity.",
