      deepMeaning: "A force applied farther from the pivot axis (larger r) produces a greater torque — this is the principle of a lever, known since Archimedes. The sinθ factor means only the perpendicular component of force contributes to rotation. A force directed straight toward the pivot produces zero torque. Torque is an axial vector (pseudovector) — it points along the axis of rotation, perpendicular to both r and F, following the right-hand rule.",
