      deepMeaning: "This theorem allows you to compute moments of inertia about any axis once you know I_cm, without repeating the full integral. It is an enormous practical tool. The md² term is always positive, which means I_cm is always the minimum moment of inertia for a given axis direction — rotation is always easiest about an axis through the center of mass.",
