      deepMeaning: "This form directly connects macroscopic pressure and volume to the microscopic count of molecules. Since N = n × N_A and R = N_A × k_B, both forms are identical. Rearranging gives P = (N/V)k_BT, so pressure depends only on the number density of molecules and temperature — not on what kind of molecules they are. Equal volumes of any ideal gas at the same T and P contain the same number of molecules. This is Avogadro's principle at the molecular level.",
      derivation: "Substitute N = n × N_A into PV = nRT, and use R = N_A × k_B: PV = (N/N_A) × N_A × k_B × T = Nk_BT.",
