      deepMeaning: "The Lorentz force on charges in the moving conductor (F = qvB) separates positive and negative charges, creating a potential difference. The EMF equals work done per unit charge: ε = vBL. Equivalently via Faraday's Law: the conductor sweeps area A = Lvt in time t → ΔΦ = BLvt → ε = BLv. Both approaches give the same result — demonstrating the deep consistency of Lorentz force and Faraday's Law. Motional EMF is the basis of all electric generators: rotating coils produce sinusoidally varying EMF — AC power.",
      derivation: "Lorentz force on each charge: F = qvB. Equilibrium when electric field E' = vB balances. Voltage across length L: ε = E'L = vBL. Or from Faraday: dΦ/dt = BL(dx/dt) = BLv → ε = BLv.",
      whoDiscovered: "Follows from Faraday's Law (1831). Faraday's first generator — the Faraday disk — was a rotating copper disk in a magnetic field, demonstrating motional EMF directly.",
