      deepMeaning: "Inductance L = NΦ/I measures flux linkage per unit current. A higher L means more flux for the same current, and more EMF induced when current changes (ε = −L dI/dt). The n² dependence means doubling turns density quadruples inductance. With ferromagnetic core: L = μ₀μᵣn²V, where μᵣ up to ~10,000 — dramatically increasing L. Units: Henry (H) = Wb/A = V·s/A. One henry induces 1 V when current changes at 1 A/s.",
